1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,418
Before astronauts land on the Moon or Mars,

2
00:00:02,748 --> 00:00:05,202
their gear is tested on Earth, but analog

3
00:00:05,214 --> 00:00:06,827
sites are picked by guesswork.

4
00:00:07,152 --> 00:00:09,732
We built PTAE: it extracts real elevation

5
00:00:09,743 --> 00:00:12,164
signatures from Moon and Mars terrain, then

6
00:00:12,175 --> 00:00:14,073
scores Earth candidates against them with

7
00:00:14,084 --> 00:00:15,936
our Analog Compatibility Index.

8
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:18,720
McMurdo Dry Valleys scores eighty-four percent

9
00:00:18,732 --> 00:00:21,550
for the lunar south pole; Mauna Kea in Hawaii

10
00:00:21,561 --> 00:00:24,289
scores a perfect one hundred percent for Jezero

11
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,209
Crater, reproducible live, in one command.

12
00:00:27,539 --> 00:00:30,209
PTAE turns guesswork into a verifiable number.
